---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Intro from '../components/Intro.astro';
import Invitation from '../components/Invitation.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="Product lab" description="Working software experiments from TemVora, with public source and clear limits.">
  <main id="main">
    <Intro label="Product lab" title="Useful tools, built from real friction." copy="Working software experiments with a focused purpose, public source, and clear limits."/>

    <section class="shell page-content product-ledger" aria-label="Current product experiments">
      <article class="product-entry">
        <div class="product-index" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
        <div class="product-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">AI VIDEO / RELEASE QA</p>
          <h2>FrameProof</h2>
          <p class="lead">Catch likely release problems before an AI-generated video leaves your desk.</p>
          <p>FrameProof samples a selected video in the browser and flags possible near-black frames, long low-motion runs, and repeated visuals for human review.</p>
          <p>It can also summarize optional ComfyUI workflow JSON and export a plain evidence report. The source video is not uploaded by the current MVP.</p>
          <a class="button" href="https://github.com/Helios56722/frameproof-ai-video-qa" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View FrameProof on GitHub <Icon name="diagonal" size={16}/></a>
        </div>
        <dl class="product-facts">
          <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Public validation MVP</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Processing</dt><dd>Local browser checks</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Does not judge</dt><dd>Story, identity, audio, or every frame</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </article>

      <article class="product-entry product-entry-new">
        <div class="product-index" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
        <div class="product-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">CLIENT DELIVERY / ACCEPTANCE</p>
          <h2>AcceptPath</h2>
          <p class="lead">Turn a scattered project handoff into a visible map of deliverables, proof, and review decisions.</p>
          <p>AcceptPath helps freelancers, consultants, technicians, and clients connect each promised result to a screenshot or delivery link, then record what was accepted and what still needs work.</p>
          <p>Evidence stays in the active browser tab. The optional AI review checks written clarity and likely mismatches; it does not inspect the finished work, interpret a contract, or make the client’s decision.</p>
          <a class="button" href="https://github.com/Helios56722/labreceipt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View AcceptPath on GitHub <Icon name="diagonal" size={16}/></a>
        </div>
        <dl class="product-facts">
          <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Local validation MVP</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Processing</dt><dd>Local evidence workspace</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Does not replace</dt><dd>Contracts, QA, or client judgment</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="shell lab-principles content-split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">THE STANDARD</p>
        <h2>Useful first.<br/><em>Honest always.</em></h2>
        <p>Each product starts with a repeated problem, a narrow promise, and enough evidence to show what the current build can actually do.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="rule-list">
        <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Keep the promise narrow.</h3><p>Describe the problem the current build handles without implying more.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Show the evidence.</h3><p>Publish the source, checks, and known limitations alongside the product.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Validate before scaling.</h3><p>Customer conversations come before paid infrastructure and complicated growth work.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <Invitation/>
  </main>
</PageLayout>
